> I am currently in the process of porting an application to Digital UNIX
> 4.0b (it's never been run on an alpha before).The app runs fine on HP/UX,
> AIX, DG/UX (motorola and Intel), AT&T/NCR.  One problem has come up on
> previous ports, that is the ability to dereference a NULL pointer. 

[... example deleted ...]

> Now this may be bad form, but I was wondering if anyone knows of a
> switch/option to allow it?

I'll skip the lecture and tell you how to make it work:

link with sys5 library, ala:

	# cc null.c -lsys5
        # a.out
	Null string = '(null)'
	Null Char = ''

The libsys5 library includes an init procedure which makes a syscall
that maps the page at address zero.    

