Yeah, that's quiet enough.

At the very least the filesystem being quotachecked shouldn't have any
other file creation activity going on at the time.  The practical
difference between being in multiuser mode with all user logins blocked
(and any other services that might write to the disk in question
disabled) and single-user mode isn't much, though.

