It is important that you supply which version of Digital Unix as well as
the compiler version. The -V compiler option will display the version.
In V3.2X and prior versions,
the c compiler is what we refer to as ACC. In V3.2C aand later V3.2
version we ship DECC which can be used with the -migrate switch.
In V4.0 and later versions, DECC is the default compiler. Also, you
should supply what flags are used. How is thr system() function
prototyped. Did you include <stdlib.h>, or
does your code supply a declaration for system().
