On Sat, 17 May 1997 11:13:32 +0300, Lefteris Tsintjelis
<lefty@csd.hol.gr> wrote:

>Would anyone expirience any core dumps when running any of the debuggers
>(dbx, ladebug, dxladebug) on a Digital Unix system running 4.0B? It
>crashes all the time after a 'continue' in any debugger.

The problem is caused by a new kernel parameter for version 4.0 called
dba_enable. The default for this parameter is 1. This causes the debug
crashes. Set the value to 0 and the problem will be solved. 

In case you are not sure how to do this, do the following: -

ladebug -k /vmunix
set dba_enable = 0 # Online, temporary fix that writes into memory.

dbx /vmunix
patch dba_enable = 0 # Permanent write to disk



