In article <5k5rkc$ais@asimov.oit.umass.edu>,
Peter deFriesse <peter@asimov.oit.umass.edu> wrote:
}  You want a DE500-AA if you have a PCI bus.  Maybe.  We just got 
}ours and lo and behold, the release notes handed us quite a surprise.
}
}  They do not work on DU versions older than 3.2g and that requires
}a patch (OSF375-048).  DU 4.0? versions should be fine (yeah, right).
}Pre-sales technical support didn't bother to mention this.

The cards work fine under 3.2D here - the firmware cannot autosense
10/100, though, so you have to explicitly set the link speed with
the 'speed' ifconfig flag. The latest firmware adds the ability to
autosense, and this firmware, of course, should only be used with the
newer OS releases.

