Michel van der List wrote:
> 
> Hi there.
> 
> I have a AlphaStation 255/233, which has a S3 Trio64 (SVGA)
> Plug-N-Play module as it's graphics board. I trying to run fvwm2
> (.0.45) on this machine, but whenever I start up fvwm2 (a public
> domain window manager), the Xserver goes into a tail spin. It
> is using up any spare cycle it can get it's hands on, seeming
> spending most of it's time in system mode as witnessed by vmubc,
> a simple digital performance monitor. Even if I later on get
> rid of fvwm, and instead use mwm, the problem persists. Logging
> out (thereby resetting the Xserver) seems to be the only way to
> get rid of this problem.
> 

Michel,

I've seen a similar problem that may or may not be related. I used to
find that emacs version 19 burnt up CPU (though still working perfectly)
whenever I ran it on the console. The X server also looped.

It turned out the problem only occurred when the DISPLAY environment
variable was set to "local:0.0".  So I edited /usr/lib/X11/xdm/Xservers
to set DISPLAY to ":0.0" .

Bob
