Greg Green (ggreen.afis@worldnet.att.net) wrote:
: How can I run a parity check on my memory in my DEC AlphaStation 255/233
: running DU 3.2c?

I dont know what/how ist tested. But in the console mode you can start:

memexer [number]

[number] Number of (parallel running) exercisers. Three to five exercisers
runs 15 minutes up to 1 hour is most sufficient for troubleshooting most
memory problems.   Says DEC.

The exerciser runs in background and nothing is displayed unless an error
occurs.

Example:

>>>>memexer 4

>>>>show_status
 
>>>>kill_diags


