>

I recently installed 4.0B and transferred code from 3.2D. It was a
total disaster. The code wouldn't recompile on 4.0B. There wasn't time
to sort the problem out properly so we just downgraded again. 

Also in a small attempt to get the code compiled, break points were
set in ladebug, which causes the system to crash!!!!!

There is an easy fix for this as a new kernel parameter (whose name I
forget at the moment) needs resetting from 1 to 0. 

This release looks flakey. Unless you really need it, stay with 3.2
which is stable. Our 4.0B system also had all the latest patches (now
called 4.0C), so there isn't currently anything better.



