From: vellani@aplcenmp.apl.jhu.edu (Thomas Vellani)
Subject: Re: NTrigue vs Wincenter anyone?
Date: 1997/05/09
Message-ID: <5l0lhp$mtq@aplcenmp.apl.jhu.edu>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 240394113
References: <5kppei$g9n@scotsman.ed.ac.uk>
Organization: The Johns Hopkins University Part-Time Programs in Engineering and Applied Science
Newsgroups: comp.os.ms-windows.networking.tcp-ip,comp.sys.sun.apps,comp.sys.hp.hpux,comp.unix.osf.osf1,comp.windows.x.apps


mitchell@sloth.ph.ed.ac.uk (Paul Mitchell) writes:

>I am looking at employing a Citrix Winframe-based product to provide access
>to Windows NT applications from NCD X-terminals, Unix workstations (Solaris,
>OSF, HPUX), and am considering the following two incarnations: NTrigue (from
>Insignia) and Wincenter (NCD).

>I'm sure someone else has done an unbiassed comparison of these two very
>similar products?  I would be extremely grateful if anyone could let me know
>what they found, in terms of performance, reliability, compatibility and/or
>Unix integration tools.

>Email preferred, I will post a summary.

>Thanks,
>Paul
	

	We have been using NCD Wincenter 2.x (NT 3.51) for more than
six months. Very satisfied with the performance. It is on a Ppro GW2000
server with 64MB of RAM. Average about nine users. Only  3-4
power users at a time . They recommend 10Mb per normal user.
It has been working great. Had to increase virtual memory. At times
it feels like it could use more memory. We got 64Mb more but
have not yet installed it since the system is performing ok
at this point.

	The X-displays are a mix of Suns & HPs workstations along
with HDS and NCD X-terminals.  Users are all part of Sun NIS domain 
and share their UNIX (Sun) home directories as H: drive. 
Wincenter authenticates logins with the NIS Sun server and NFS 
mounts their home directory. 

Users  who have floppy drive at their local display gets to use it 
as a: drive. LPD Print spooling is done like the UNIX, some of
them direct to Jetdirect LPD hosts and others via UNIX spoolers.  
This has been a blessing for all the UNIX users who get occassional
wintel mail attachments. Use their NIS login and print or view
mail attachments. Installed Sun Solstice IMAP mail client on the
Wincenter and works fine along with regular MS applications.

	We have ordered a upgrade to new version 3.0 the other day. 
It has NIS,NIS+ and NFS3 support. It is still based on NT 3.51. I was told
the version based on NT 4.0 is in advanced beta and should be out
by the end of Summer. I see hope for NCs :) if "you know who" won't
dry up the licenses to NCD and Insignia . I heard there has been
spike in the license fee already.

	I haven't had any experience with NTrigue.

-tom
vellani@jhuapl.edu



