Hi,
I am having a problem with a large X app running on both Alphastation
255's and 500's with Digital Unix 3.2C and 3.2D.   This application
uses Xt and the Athena wigets. No motif.    The app displays 2D graphics
screens and is used contiuously.   The problem is that when there is a 
large amount of graphical data random windows pop up with random fields 
blank.  A mouse click in the field will fix this, also iconizing an bringing
back the window.   This fault never happened on the earlier Alpha 3000
machines running OSF/1.

I used the xmon program to look at the events for a window that pops up ok
and one that has some blank fields,  I found that for the good window all
expose events occur and then the text is updated in the fields.  For the
