Not sure exactly what you mean by not mounted. The CD-ROM can be
accessed from the ARC console by specifying the appropriate address. You
can look around the ARC console, and it will show the devices.

>
> 2)  What is ARC?  For that matter, what is the SRM colsole?  I've
> never
> used either.  Maybe I have and just never heard of it refert to as
> such.  Is there a man page describing it?  If not... how do I use
> it?

There is not a man page since the console is hardware. The SRM is The
System Reference Manual console which is the standard boot prompt for DU
and VMS, eg. the one with >>>>>
You can get to the ARC console by setting your OS type to Windows NT.
There is online documentation for SRM via the help command, and there is
a reference manual that is shipped with some systems. The ARC console is
a menu driven console. Relatively easy to navigate. As mentioned
earlier, you can address any device on the system directly.  (eg.
scsi(0)cdrom(5)).
Also, there is an undocumented and unsupported way you can get to the
ARC console from the SRM console. At the console prompt, just type ARC.

One word of caution is that the system time format is different in the
two console modes, so in ARC, you will always need to fix the time.
