Jean-Claude Magras wrote:
> but I get this insistent error before many others....
> NODE.h:98: field `IPsocket' has incomplete type
> 

This is probably because you have not given a forward declaration of U,
the type of IPsocket.  This is not sufficient since you are trying to
instantiate an object IPsocket, of type U.  The compiler MUST know how
much memory it has to allocate for the object, the objects in the class
U (if any), etc.  You have to include the class definition of U before
you can instantiate any object of type U.

Hope this helps.

