You don't say which version of D.U. you are running. Under V3.2G, I've
always used "netsetup" and answered the questions. It appears that the
default router information is in /etc/routes. You need a line:

default 192.168.1.2

in this file. The command:

route add default 192.168.1.2 

should work, but if my understanding is right the information will not
be preserved across a reboot.
