Regarding my earlier posting: We have just received a fix from DEC that
now allows us to use DCE authentication (with the SIA integrated login)
and still have unexposed (encrypted) password entries.  The solution
entailed setting the d_accept_alternate_vouching flag in the
/etc/auth/system/default file and then getting a correct
/etc/sia/matrix.conf file.  Next week I will be testing this solution to
see the extent of the integration.  We already have AIX machines
running integrated login and our common DCE environment is growing.

