Well I can't do a comparison, cuz I only use NTrigue. But so far NTrigue has 
been very reliable, compatible, and better performing than Wabi or SoftWindows. 
I am running NTrigue3.0  on a Pentium/90 w/64 MB and 6 BG disk...it's a system 
we put together from scraps. Wih 6 users running Word/Excel/Visio/TKSolver, it 
still performs better than a local copy of Wabi or SoftWindows on a 715/50. 

The only compatibility problems I have seen are NT-related, not NTrigue 
related. I had a problem with McAfee NetShield for NT. I heard that other NT 
users were having problems with this also. The new 3.0 of NetShield does not 
recognize NTrigue as a valid 3.51 server, so won't install. I am still trying 
to figure that one out.

The other problem i had was with some software license metering s/w. It could 
meter licenses of software that were checked out from the NT server, but could 
not if they were actually RUNNING ON the NT server, which of course they do 
with NTrigue. So I couldn't do software metering on NTrigue, at least until the 
metering vendor removs this limitation. Otherwise, all my apps are working 
beautifully.

The only other problem I have with NTrigue is their expensive support. The 
support I have gotten was pretty good, but pricey. 

