In <33682CFD.778E7E2A@wam.umd.edu> Jens Dreger <dreger@wam.umd.edu> writes:
>I'm trying to compile the tiff-library ver3.4 on an Alpha Station,
>OSF1 V3.2 41.64 alpha. (ftp.sgi.com/graphics/tiff-v3.4-tar.gz).
>I get an error of the form
>[...]
>Unresolved:
>__eprintf
>*** Exit 1
>Stop.
>I tried it on different alpha's (V4.0), but always got this message.
>Please let me know, if you have any idea what's wrong here...

As far as I know, __eprintf is part of the GCC assertion handling.
You need to compile *and* link programs that use GCC assertion 
handlink with gcc.

__eprintf is used in /usr/local/alpha-dec-osf3.2/include/assert.h
and defined in /usr/local/lib/gcc-lib/alpha-dec-osf3.2/2.7.2/libgcc.a
(paths vary on installation).

