Greg Green wrote:
> 
> I need to remove specific directories from a particular subdirectory.  I
> tried using the command rm -rfi filename* and I was prompted with:
> 
>         bash: /sbin/rm: Arg list too long
> 
> Is there a way around this?  Is there a way to increase the size for
> this list even temporarily?  Must I delete one directory at a time until
> I get the list small enough?

You can do it in three ways:
1. If you want to delete all subdirs, go up one level and to rm -r
topdir.

2. Delete smaller number of directories at a time. I often manually have
to do "rm -r a*", "rm -r b*" etc.

3. Use find: "find . -name "filename*" -type d -exec rm -r {} \;".

Good luck.

/Marek



