In article <336D0DD3.28551810@ramius.demon.co.uk>, Mark Nelson
<mark@ramius.demon.co.uk> wrote:

>I'm trying to port a program from a sun running 4.1.3 to OSF1, the 
>uname output of the development machine is OSF1 leo V3.2 41 alpha and 
>the output of the uname command machine on which the program will
>eventually
>run is OSF1 scorpio.tees.ac.uk V3.2 148 alpha.
>
>To access the quota information I am using the quotactl system call,
>which 
>according to the man page it takes the following parameters - 
>
>quotactl(device,QCMD(GETQUOTA,USRQUOTA),uid,&quota);
>
>Unfortunatly when I run the program I get error 22 returned when I 
>try to do a getquota call.  Below is the output of program -
>
># df /usr
>Filesystem   512-blocks        Used       Avail Capacity  Mounted on
>/dev/rz0g       1603526     1126522      316650    78%    /usr
># ./a.out /dev/rz0g cmt17 1 3
>417
>-2147404728 1023
>3 1
>setting Quota
>error 22 returned from quotactl(Q_SETQUOTA)

You are going to kick yourself.

The man page says

  path      Specifies the pathname of any file within the mounted file sys-
            tem.

You specified the device, _NOT_ a file _WITHIN_ the mounted file system.

Change your command line to 

    ./a.out /usr cmt17 1 3

and you should make forward progress in debugging your program.

I have not looked at your code, so I don't know if there are any other
problems or if you are all set now.

